{
  "dom_id": "step-q344566",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}cos\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14252450/assets/86c0cf22de78e3b773543680c2ace077f97b66ae822436d637c5444903e2330f.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}cos\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)) & =cos\\,(arctan\\,(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =cos\\,(arctan\\,(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
